          "text": "UML has its roots in object-oriented design. Its class diagrams are particularly useful for Information Mapping. The ArchiMate Specification’s representation of business objects and their relationships owes a lot to UML, basically being a less detailed model and omitting things like methods, attributes, and relationship cardinalities.",
